Once upon a time, there was a little boy named Ravi who lived in a small village. Every morning, he helped his father in the fields and went to school in the afternoon.

One day, Ravi found a small bird lying under a tree. The bird had a broken wing and could not fly. Ravi gently picked it up and took it home. He gave the bird some water and placed it in a small box with soft cloth.

Every day, Ravi cared for the bird and gave it food. After a few weeks, the bird became healthy and started flying around the house.

One morning, Ravi opened the window, and the bird flew into the sky. Ravi felt happy because he had helped a little creature return to its home.

His father smiled and said, "Kindness is one of the greatest gifts you can give to the world."

From that day onward, Ravi always helped people and animals whenever he could.

Moral: A small act of kindness can make a big difference.
